WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
Let's make Fallen-leaf animal pictures.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.059
Arrange fallen leaves into a fox, owl or bird, then tape them to a

3
00:00:07.059 --> 00:00:07.920
sheet of card.

4
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.460
Draw small features with a crayon.

5
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.920
Make this project with a grown-up.

6
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.030
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

7
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.655
Pause whenever you need more time.

8
00:00:19.035 --> 00:00:22.485
An adult checks plants and helps tape delicate pieces.

9
00:00:22.865 --> 00:00:25.655
Avoid berries, seeds or tiny loose eyes.

10
00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:28.357
Step 1.

11
00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:30.502
Look for animal shapes.

12
00:00:30.882 --> 00:00:33.117
Spread the leaves beside the card.

13
00:00:33.497 --> 00:00:37.565
Find a broad body leaf, a smaller head leaf and two shapes for ears,

14
00:00:37.565 --> 00:00:38.727
wings or a tail.

15
00:00:39.107 --> 00:00:42.167
Turn leaves around to see new possibilities.

16
00:00:42.547 --> 00:00:43.927
Grown-up help.

17
00:00:44.307 --> 00:00:46.152
Check all collected leaves.

18
00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:48.847
Step 2.

19
00:00:49.227 --> 00:00:50.707
Start with the body.

20
00:00:51.087 --> 00:00:54.092
Place the largest leaf in the middle of the card.

21
00:00:54.472 --> 00:00:58.331
Add the head leaf above or beside it, leaving a little room for ears

22
00:00:58.331 --> 00:00:58.882
or wings.

23
00:00:59.262 --> 00:01:00.517
Do not tape yet.

24
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.345
Step 3.

25
00:01:03.725 --> 00:01:05.725
Add ears, wings or a tail.

26
00:01:06.105 --> 00:01:08.690
Try the smaller leaves around the body.

27
00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.355
Two pointed leaves can be ears; two rounded leaves can be wings.

28
00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:17.335
Move the pieces until the animal is easy to recognise.

29
00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:19.984
Step 4.

30
00:01:20.364 --> 00:01:22.239
Fix the leaves in place.

31
00:01:22.619 --> 00:01:24.639
Lift one leaf at a time.

32
00:01:25.019 --> 00:01:28.849
Make a small loop of tape, sticky side out, and press it onto the

33
00:01:28.849 --> 00:01:29.944
back of the leaf.

34
00:01:30.324 --> 00:01:32.694
Put the leaf back and press gently.

35
00:01:33.074 --> 00:01:35.124
Tape stems flat if needed.

36
00:01:35.504 --> 00:01:36.884
Grown-up help.

37
00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:40.199
Make tape loops and help attach fragile leaves.

38
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:42.842
Step 5.

39
00:01:43.222 --> 00:01:45.287
Draw the finishing details.

40
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:49.202
Draw eyes, a nose and feet on the card beside the leaf shapes.

41
00:01:49.582 --> 00:01:52.047
Add a name or a little habitat picture.

42
00:01:52.427 --> 00:01:55.152
Keep the artwork flat while the leaves dry.

43
00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:56.912
Grown-up help.

44
00:01:57.292 --> 00:01:59.477
Check there are no loose pieces.

45
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.915
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

46
00:02:04.295 --> 00:02:07.845
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

47
00:02:08.225 --> 00:02:10.245
Your creation can look different.

48
00:02:10.625 --> 00:02:13.845
Remove leaves and tape before sorting materials.

49
00:02:14.225 --> 00:02:18.540
Display flat indoors and expect leaves to change shape as they dry.

50
00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:19.910
Well done.

51
00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.720
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

